{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "792e1fd3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Building Defect AI — Notebook workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "Run from the repository root. Expected data layout: `dataset/BD3_split/{train,val,test}/<class_name>/...`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** classify images into the seven BD3 labels. This notebook records the method, why it is used, the result and its interpretation. Do not treat model predictions as professional inspection findings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f7c864e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets, models\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "DATA = ROOT / \"dataset\" / \"BD3_split\"\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(\"Project:\", ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Device:\", DEVICE)\n",
    "assert DATA.exists(), f\"Dataset folder not found: {DATA}. Run from the project root and add the dataset.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a056e9f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. ResNet18 preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "The pretrained ResNet18 weights provide their recommended transforms. These resize/crop and normalise images to the distribution expected by the ImageNet-pretrained backbone. Consistent preprocessing at training and inference is essential."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eedf1c3b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "weights = models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT\n",
    "transform = weights.transforms()\n",
    "train_ds = datasets.ImageFolder(DATA / \"train\", transform=transform)\n",
    "loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=16, shuffle=True, num_workers=0)\n",
    "images, labels = next(iter(loader))\n",
    "print(\"Image batch:\", images.shape)  # [batch, channels, height, width]\n",
    "print(\"Label batch:\", labels.shape)  # [batch]\n",
    "print(\"First label:\", train_ds.classes[labels[0].item()])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5246498",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Inspect a preprocessed image\n",
    "\n",
    "Normalisation changes displayed pixel values. For a quick visual check, display the original PIL image from the dataset rather than plotting the normalised tensor directly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4548dee6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "path, label = train_ds.samples[0]\n",
    "img = Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(5,5)); plt.imshow(img); plt.title(train_ds.classes[label]); plt.axis(\"off\"); plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d2d10b22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Why batches?\n",
    "\n",
    "A batch groups multiple images into one tensor so the GPU can process them efficiently. With batch size 16 and ResNet18 input size 224×224, the expected tensor shape is `[16, 3, 224, 224]` (the final batch may be smaller)."
   ]
  }
 ],
